# The three original source documents stay local. docs/ is now published: it holds the
# results analysis, the forward plan, the security programme, the survey and the model
# explainer. README.md is the repo's own documentation and IS tracked.
semantic-communication-roadmap.md
semcom-roadmap-expansion.md
semcom-walkthrough-for-ml-readers.md

# Results: track the run records, never the weights. history.json / config.yaml /
# ablation.json are a few KB each and are the provenance of every reported number, so
# they belong in the repo. best.pt and checkpoint.pt are ~40 MB each and would add
# ~650 MB per sweep, permanently, since git keeps every version forever.
#
# Written as "ignore the contents, then re-include by extension" rather than "results/":
# once a directory itself is excluded git never descends into it, so a negation inside an
# excluded directory has no effect. The "!results/**/" line is what lets git look inside.
results/**
!results/**/
!results/**/*.json
!results/**/*.yaml
!results/**/*.png
!results/**/*.pdf
!results/**/*.csv

data/
wandb/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/

.claude/

# Stray editor/tool artifacts
tea_debug.log
*.log
